        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                "word": "hypocondrie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "546e5b4f-a185-4ddb-aa15-4c6833aa617d",
                        "entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hypocondries"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4c91090c-ff56-433b-9688-dce6b1994b33",
                        "entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "hypochondrie"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1434e9ec-7c52-327d-8f0d-3d4376068535",
                        "entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Trouble psychiatrique dans lequel on se plaint fréquemment de l’impression d’avoir une maladie grave, de douleurs variées ou de souffrances excessives malgré les apparences d’une bonne santé."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87a4fed4-84b4-48d6-ab95-2a6bf9d96ff2",
                                "sense_id": "1434e9ec-7c52-327d-8f0d-3d4376068535",
                                "text": "L’espèce d’hypocondrie froide et élégante qui perçait dans toute sa personne prouvait que si quelque chose survivait au découragement de beaucoup d’ambitions si vulgaires, c’était à la fois le dégoût de lui-même avec l’amour excessif du bien-être."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ec7e60f-95b8-485d-90c7-866bbb55fbde",
                                "sense_id": "1434e9ec-7c52-327d-8f0d-3d4376068535",
                                "text": "Dans « le Conflit des facultés », au chapitre hypocondrie, Kant confesse : « Pour moi, j’ai, à cause de ma poitrine plate et étroite, qui laisse peu de place au mouvement du cœur et du poumon, une disposition naturelle à l’hypocondrie qui allait jadis jusqu’à un dégout de vivre »."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6bba5253-04cc-388f-8dc0-a59d5c8f4c48",
                        "entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "État d'une personne qui craint la maladie de façon obsessive ou qui se croit abusivement malade sous tous prétextes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a33d961-8ee9-4424-ab5b-71d4db76d3ee",
                                "sense_id": "6bba5253-04cc-388f-8dc0-a59d5c8f4c48",
                                "text": "Rien qu'à l'idée d'attraper le virus, la personne atteinte de cette maladie mentale, l'hypocondrie, développe une anxiété excessive. Elle est persuadée qu'elle développe les symptômes de la contamination (perte du goût, de l'odorat, fièvre...)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a894fef8-1c99-3da9-8ee9-66411626e93b",
                        "entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Espèce de mélancolie ou de tristesse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76ecadd1-3025-4a40-9725-51be490440b8",
                                "sense_id": "a894fef8-1c99-3da9-8ee9-66411626e93b",
                                "text": "Une sombre hypocondrie."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "10cd1477-bd41-4167-8c46-863644b99580",
                                "sense_id": "a894fef8-1c99-3da9-8ee9-66411626e93b",
                                "text": "N’ayant plus à molester aucun chenapan, sa tristesse fut infinie et devint presque aussitôt une hypocondrie des plus noires."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "532fd1a8-40e2-4b5b-8564-632c749c3d74",
                        "source_entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "target_lang_word": "Hypochondrie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Hypochondrie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "431a9fd9-4acb-3dd4-a87f-93ebe9ded3c5",
                                        "entry_id": "57dab398-8f5c-3aa5-9cd2-70d9e1cf3cb4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "übertriebene, anhaltende, unbegründete Angst vor ernsthaften Krankheiten; psychische Verfassung eines Hypochonders"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e67dc89-ee08-48ee-92a0-c70ebb00c9ee",
                                                "sense_id": "431a9fd9-4acb-3dd4-a87f-93ebe9ded3c5",
                                                "text": "„Es kann nicht erklären, wie es sich fühlt, aber es kann auch nicht lügen, sich Symptome zurechtmachen oder sich den Freuden der Hypochondrie ergeben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a658cf0f-cca0-4383-86bd-3883a858567f",
                                                "sense_id": "431a9fd9-4acb-3dd4-a87f-93ebe9ded3c5",
                                                "text": "„Wir neigen zur Hypochondrie, das heißt, wir hören auf die leisesten Signale unserer Alarmanlagen, auch weil wir fürchten, dass sie ständig Schlimmes ankündigen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "872de4ad-18f9-4bff-8463-d46c2847d76f",
                                                "sense_id": "431a9fd9-4acb-3dd4-a87f-93ebe9ded3c5",
                                                "text": "„Pierre fühlte seit dem Balle wieder einen Anfall von Hypochondrie sich vorbereiten, dem er mit verzweifelter Anstrengung zu wehren trachtete.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea302188-c6d1-4153-a3fe-ce40bed318df",
                                                "sense_id": "431a9fd9-4acb-3dd4-a87f-93ebe9ded3c5",
                                                "text": "„Nichts hätte in seinem Fall näher gelegen, als der Hypochondrie zu verfallen, da er wegen seiner flachen und nicht sehr ausgedehnten Brust regelmäßig unter Herzbeklemmungen litt.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e5bd296f-400c-448b-b174-2a86a03bcc0b",
                        "source_entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "target_lang_word": "hypochondria",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypochondria",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ca3251e-6cc3-365b-a067-ee3d0ad72233",
                                        "entry_id": "912a0490-cb07-3a18-8f2e-7b68fda10aea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A formerly defined psychological disorder characterized by excessive preoccupation or worry about having a serious illness. No longer a current medical diagnosis; see hypochondriasis for more."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb67e952-5407-4adf-b271-96878b46b534",
                                                "sense_id": "4ca3251e-6cc3-365b-a067-ee3d0ad72233",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: hypochondriasis"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c382af38-4233-338f-abe8-af59c497d535",
                                        "entry_id": "912a0490-cb07-3a18-8f2e-7b68fda10aea",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Melancholy; depression."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0df971b-886d-462d-8cf9-f8038eb49be9",
                                                "sense_id": "c382af38-4233-338f-abe8-af59c497d535",
                                                "text": "Such labours as these, if they do not shorten life, are calculated to make it wretched, for hypochondria invariably follows close upon them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc7e0746-cbeb-42a6-ba7b-9fe013f38819",
                                                "sense_id": "c382af38-4233-338f-abe8-af59c497d535",
                                                "text": "His own temperament appears to have been neither purely sanguine, choleric, phlegmatic, nor melancholic [...] not melancholy, since he is entirely free from hypochondria, thinks rapidly, and has an active will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8d647c2-c6b9-42dc-bc7e-d9fb9714d4df",
                                                "sense_id": "c382af38-4233-338f-abe8-af59c497d535",
                                                "text": "Nux likewise corresponds to hypochondria caused by rich and excessive living. In general, Nux is the best remedy for hypochondria arising from a morbid condition of the abdominal nerves ; after dinner, the patients generally experience a feeling of malaise and langour."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypochondria",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "377ca134-6fa9-3134-b0b7-511611a3c3c9",
                                        "entry_id": "e7a68669-0281-3fbd-a544-3a963f73f273",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "plural of hypochondrium"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "89f608e4-6b5d-4f5b-acef-4d25bd6545fe",
                        "source_entry_id": "c1394648-ffb1-3ec8-adc1-be1f97f58dd9",
                        "target_lang_word": "hypochondriasis",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypochondriasis",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65195bbd-1f5c-3faf-9764-128891415dbc",
                                        "entry_id": "5c31ef41-8c1d-3e33-9fcb-6ba7083305bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mental disorder (in some classifications of such disorders, including ICD-11) that is characterized by excessive fear of or preoccupation with a serious illness, despite medical testing and reassurance to the contrary."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f058b9e9-785f-47d5-be68-f3b8fabc9aac",
                                                "sense_id": "65195bbd-1f5c-3faf-9764-128891415dbc",
                                                "text": "Near-synonym: hypochondria"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fb3411b7-ae61-4a9c-8c78-32abfc5a7b41",
                                                "sense_id": "65195bbd-1f5c-3faf-9764-128891415dbc",
                                                "text": "Most individuals who previously would have been diagnosed with hypochondriasis in DSM-IV [1994] (preoccupation with having a serious disease based on the individual’s misinterpretation of bodily symptoms) are now classified as having somatic symptom disorder; however, in one-third of cases, the diagnosis of illness anxiety disorder applies instead."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
